<%#
  Rendered on every single page via view_layouts_base_body_top (see
  lib/custom_decrement_field/hooks.rb's InconsistencyBannerHook) - there
  is no hook that fires only on an issue's own show page and nowhere
  else, so `controller` (part of every hook's call context - see
  Redmine::Hook::Helper#call_hook) is checked by hand below, and every
  page this doesn't apply to falls out at this first check without
  rendering anything.
%>
<%
  issue = if controller.is_a?(IssuesController) && controller.action_name == 'show'
            controller.instance_variable_get(:@issue)
          end
  calculators = if issue.is_a?(Issue) && issue.persisted?
                  CustomDecrementField::StockCalculator.calculators_for(issue).select(&:inconsistent?)
                else
                  []
                end
%>
<% if calculators.any? %>
  <%#
    The same "Note #N" numbering core itself shows next to every comment
    (see Issue#visible_journals_with_index, used the same way by
    IssuesController#show to build @journals) - built the same way here,
    rather than numbering duplicate_literals' own journals directly, so
    that a duplicate whose second occurrence is a private note the
    current user isn't allowed to see simply gets no link below, instead
    of linking to a note they can't actually open.
  %>
  <% numbered_journals = issue.visible_journals_with_index(User.current).index_by(&:id) %>
  <%#
    Rendered `hidden`, then moved into #content and revealed by the
    script below, once the DOM has actually parsed that far - see the
    script's own comment for why this can't just render there directly.
    Hiding it until that move (rather than leaving it visible where it
    lands via view_layouts_base_body_top - the very top of <body>, above
    even Redmine's own top menu and header) is what keeps a page load
    from ever showing the banner in the wrong place for an instant before
    JS relocates it.
  %>
  <div id="custom-decrement-field-inconsistency-banner" class="custom-decrement-field-inconsistency-banner" hidden>
    <p class="custom-decrement-field-inconsistency-banner-title">
      <%= l(:text_custom_decrement_field_inconsistent_title) %>
    </p>
    <ul>
      <% calculators.each do |calculator| %>
        <li>
          <strong><%= calculator.field.name %></strong>
          <ul>
            <% if calculator.negative? %>
              <li><%= l(:text_custom_decrement_field_inconsistent_negative, value: calculator.value) %></li>
            <% end %>
            <% calculator.duplicate_literals.each do |literal, journals| %>
              <li>
                <%= l(:text_custom_decrement_field_inconsistent_duplicate, literal: literal) %>
                <%
                  links = journals.filter_map { |journal| numbered_journals[journal.id] }
                                   .sort_by(&:indice)
                                   .map { |journal| link_to("##{journal.indice}", "#note-#{journal.indice}") }
                %>
                <% if links.any? %>
                  (<%= safe_join(links, ', ') %>)
                <% end %>
              </li>
            <% end %>
          </ul>
        </li>
      <% end %>
    </ul>
  </div>
  <%#
    view_layouts_base_body_top (see hooks.rb) is the only hook that fires
    above any of a page's own content at all - but that puts this banner
    above Redmine's own top menu and header too, not just above the
    issue, which reads as the banner belonging to the whole application
    rather than to this one ticket. There is no hook that fires later -
    specifically between the top of #content and the issue's own heading
    (verified against 6.0-stable's app/views/layouts/base.html.erb and
    app/views/issues/show.html.erb - see hooks.rb's own comment) - so this
    moves the banner there itself once the DOM includes #content, rather
    than rendering it there to begin with.

    DOMContentLoaded, not immediately: at the point this script tag is
    parsed, #content does not exist yet in the DOM (base.html.erb draws
    it much later than <body>'s own opening tag) - `content` below would
    be null and the move would silently fail.

    If JavaScript is disabled or blocked, this banner simply never
    appears - that is an accepted degradation, not a silent failure to
    warn: the small marker next to the field's own value
    (DecrementableIntFormat#inconsistency_marker), the row highlighting
    in list/query views (IssueCssClassesPatch), and the query filter
    (IssueQueryPatch) are all still fully server-rendered and need no
    JavaScript at all.
  %>
  <script>
    document.addEventListener('DOMContentLoaded', function () {
      var banner = document.getElementById('custom-decrement-field-inconsistency-banner');
      if (!banner) return;

      var content = document.getElementById('content');
      if (content) content.insertBefore(banner, content.firstChild);
      banner.hidden = false;
    });
  </script>
<% end %>
